    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d92">

                <pb facs="0097" n="85" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg85"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/16294</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Secretary of
                        State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-10-29">October 29, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The British Ambassador called at his request. He brought up the Finnish question
                    and stated that Russia desired Great Britain to declare war against Finland. I
                    disposed of the matter by saying that on yesterday I had sent a strong message
                    to the Finnish Government bringing this matter as nearly to a sharp focus as
                    possible short of a breach of relations, and paving the way for any further
                    action at any time. This seemed to satisfy the Ambassador for the present.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ordell</hi>] H[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >ull</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
